[22.14904, "o", "Found the core problem. Let me confirm a couple of details before repairing.\r\n"]
[22.179522, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mecho \"== dist-info contents ==\"; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info; echo; echo \"== RECORD head ==\"; head -5 /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/RECORD 2>&1; echo; echo \"== other python ==\"; /usr/bin/python3 --version 2>&1; /usr/bin/python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; echo; echo \"== sitecustomize/pth ==\"; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/*.pth /usr/local/lib/python3.13/sitecustomize.py 2>&1; echo; echo \"== disk ==\"; df -h /usr/local 2>&1\r\n== dist-info contents ==\r\ntotal 112\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Jan 14  2025 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Oct 31 13:45 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 10925 Jan 14  2025 AUTHORS.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     4 Jan 14  2025 INSTALLER\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1093 Jan 14  2025 LICENSE.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  3677 Jan 14  2025 METADATA\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 65525 Jan 14  2025 RECORD\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     0 Jan 14  2025 REQUESTED\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    91 Jan 14  2025 WHEEL\r\n-rw-r--r-"]
[22.179692, "o", "- 1 root root    87 Jan 14  2025 entry_points.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     4 Jan 14  2025 top_level.txt\r\n\r\n== RECORD head ==\r\n../../../bin/pip3,sha256=0b9s6uF-112mlJv1gtUrMFJh6BKXbpJf0_WlXw7hrMo,230\r\r\n../../../bin/pip3.13,sha256=0b9s6uF-112mlJv1gtUrMFJh6BKXbpJf0_WlXw7hrMo,230\r\r\npip-24.3.1.dist-info/AUTHORS.txt,sha256=Cbb630k8EL9FkBzX9Vpi6hpYWrLSlh08eXodL5u0eLI,10925\r\r\npip-24.3.1.dist-info/INSTALLER,sha256=zuuue4knoyJ-UwPPXg8fezS7VCrXJQrAP7zeNuwvFQg,4\r\r\npip-24.3.1.dist-info/LICENSE.txt,sha256=Y0MApmnUmurmWxLGxIySTFGkzfPR_whtw0VtyLyqIQQ,1093\r\r\n\r\n== other python ==\r\nPython 3.11.2\r\n/usr/bin/python3: No module named pip\r\n\r\n== sitecustomize/pth ==\r\nls: cannot access '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/*.pth': No such file or directory\r\nls: cannot access '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/sitecustomize.py': No such file or directory\r\n\r\n== disk ==\r\nFilesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\r\noverlay         1.8T  1.5T  221G  88% /\r\n"]
[22.205247, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mecho \"== ensurepip bundle ==\"; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/ 2>&1; echo; echo \"== import test ==\"; python3 -c \"import importlib.util; print(importlib.util.find_spec('pip'))\" 2>&1; echo; echo \"== sysconfig purelib ==\"; python3 -c \"import sysconfig; print(sysconfig.get_paths()['purelib'])\" 2>&1\r\n== ensurepip bundle ==\r\ntotal 1792\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root    4096 Jan 14  2025 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root    4096 Jan 14  2025 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1822182 Jan 14  2025 pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\n\r\n== import test ==\r\nNone\r\n\r\n== sysconfig purelib ==\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages\r\n"]
[23.199103, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[26.557578, "o", "Diagnosis is clear: the `pip/` package directory was deleted from `site-packages`, but its `.dist-info` and the `/usr/local/bin/pip*` launcher scripts were left behind. That's why `pip` says \"No module named pip\". Let me reinstall it from Python's bundled wheel.\r\n"]
[27.638486, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\"\r\nLooking in links: /tmp/tmp8inaaikv\r\nRequirement already satisfied: pip in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages (24.3.1)\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your system unusable.It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what you are doing and want to suppress this warning.\r\nEXIT=0\r\n"]
[28.760981, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[32.196815, "o", "`ensurepip` short-circuited because the leftover `.dist-info` still claims pip is installed. I'll move that stale metadata aside and re-run it so the wheel actually gets unpacked.\r\n"]
[33.358365, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mset -e\r\nSP=/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages\r\nmkdir -p /tmp/opencode/pip-repair-backup\r\nmv \"$SP/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\" /tmp/opencode/pip-repair-backup/ 2>/dev/null || true\r\necho \"moved dist-info aside\"\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1\r\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\r\nmoved dist-info aside\r\nLooking in links: /tmp/tmpmd11fxqk\r\nProcessing /tmp/tmpmd11fxqk/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\nInstalling collected packages: pip\r\nSuccessfully installed pip-24.3.1\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your system unusable.It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what you are doing and want to suppress this warning.\r\nEXIT=0\r\n"]
[34.035282, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[35.672109, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /tmp && timeout 60 python3 -m pip install --dry-run six 2>&1 | tail -20; echo \"EXIT=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\r\nCollecting six\r\n  Downloading six-1.17.0-py2.py3-none-any.whl.metadata (1.7 kB)\r\nDownloading six-1.17.0-py2.py3-none-any.whl (11 kB)\r\nWould install six-1.17.0\r\n\r\n[notice] A new release of pip is available: 24.3.1 -> 26.2.2\r\n[notice] To update, run: pip install --upgrade pip\r\nEXIT=0\r\n"]
[35.864701, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpython3 -m pip --version 2>&1; echo \"---\"; pip --version 2>&1; echo \"---\"; pip3 --version 2>&1; echo \"---IMPORT---\"; python3 -c \"import pip, pip._internal.cli.main; print('pip imports OK:', pip.__version__)\" 2>&1\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n---\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n---\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n---IMPORT---\r\npip imports OK: 24.3.1\r\n"]
[36.626634, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[39.531725, "o", "`pip` is working again and can reach PyPI. Let me verify an actual install writes correctly, and check the secondary system Python.\r\n"]
[39.562281, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mecho \"== /usr/bin/python3 (3.11) ==\"; /usr/bin/python3 -m ensurepip --version 2>&1; echo \"---apt pip pkg---\"; dpkg -l 2>/dev/null | grep -iE '^ii\\s+(python3-pip|python3\\.11-venv)' || echo \"python3-pip not installed via dpkg\"; echo \"---ensurepip module---\"; ls -d /usr/lib/python3.11/ensurepip 2>&1\r\n== /usr/bin/python3 (3.11) ==\r\n/usr/bin/python3: No module named ensurepip\r\n---apt pip pkg---\r\npython3-pip not installed via dpkg\r\n---ensurepip module---\r\nls: cannot access '/usr/lib/python3.11/ensurepip': No such file or directory\r\n"]
[39.885251, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mrm -rf /tmp/opencode/pip-test && timeout 90 python3 -m pip install --quiet --target /tmp/opencode/pip-test six 2>&1; echo \"install exit=$?\"; PYTHONPATH=/tmp/opencode/pip-test python3 -c \"import six; print('six import OK:', six.__version__)\" 2>&1\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your system unusable.It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what you are doing and want to suppress this warning.\r\n\r\n[notice] A new release of pip is available: 24.3.1 -> 26.2.2\r\n[notice] To update, run: pip install --upgrade pip\r\ninstall exit=0\r\nsix import OK: 1.17.0\r\n"]
[41.43479, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[43.909664, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mrm -rf /tmp/opencode/pip-test; echo \"cleaned test dir\"; echo \"--- final site-packages state ---\"; ls -d /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info 2>&1; echo \"--- launchers ---\"; ls -l /usr/local/bin/pip /usr/local/bin/pip3 /usr/local/bin/pip3.13 2>&1\r\ncleaned test dir\r\n--- final site-packages state ---\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\n--- launchers ---\r\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 227 Nov  1 01:17 /usr/local/bin/pip\r\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 227 Nov  1 01:17 /usr/local/bin/pip3\r\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 227 Nov  1 01:17 /usr/local/bin/pip3.13\r\n"]
[44.850748, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[46.765154, "o", "Fixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\nYour `pip` launchers were intact, but the actual `pip` Python package had been deleted from disk:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/          <-- missing\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/  <-- orphaned leftover\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo every `pip` command died with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe leftover `.dist-info` also made `python3 -m ensurepip` wrongly report *\"Requirement already satisfied\"* and skip the repair.\r\n\r\n## What I did\r\n\r\n1. Moved the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata to `/tmp/opencode/pip-repair-backup/`.\r\n2. Reinstalled pip from Python's own bundled wheel: `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip`.\r\n\r\n## Verified working\r\n\r\n- `pip`, `pip3`, and `python3 -m pip` all report `pip 24.3.1` (Python 3.13.1).\r\n- `pip install --dry-run six` successfully resolved and downloaded from PyPI.\r\n- A real install to a temp target downloaded, installed, and imported clean"]
[46.765339, "o", "ly.\r\n\r\nThere was no `pip.conf`, proxy, or environment variable interfering — it was purely the missing package directory.\r\n\r\n## One thing to be aware of\r\n\r\nYou have a *second* Python at `/usr/bin/python3` (Debian 3.11.2). It has no pip and no `ensurepip` module, and `python3-pip` isn't installed via dpkg. That's normal for a minimal Debian image rather than \"broken.\" If you want pip there too, it should be installed through apt rather than ensurepip:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\napt-get update && apt-get install -y python3-pip python3.11-venv\r\n```\r\n\r\nWant me to set that one up as well? Also note the deletion happened recently (site-packages was modified Oct 31), so if this is a container image build, whatever cleaned that directory may do it again.\r\n"]
[46.948247, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e289183e6aae:/app# "]
[52.011912, "i", "\u0004"]
[52.012079, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n"]
[52.012109, "o", "exit\r\n"]
